@startuml 01b-docker-variant
title pi-gen stock Docker path (upstream default — NOT used by ivaliceCluster)

skinparam defaultFontName Menlo
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor Black
    LifeLineBorderColor Black
    ParticipantBorderColor Black
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
}

actor Operator
participant "build-docker.sh" as BD
participant "Docker daemon" as Docker
participant "pi-gen container\n(debian:trixie)" as Container
database "pi-gen/deploy/" as Deploy

note over Operator, Deploy
  Provided as reference only. Upstream pi-gen's default way to build
  on a machine with Docker. It does NOT satisfy ivaliceCluster's needs
  (see "why it doesn't work for us" notes), which is why we use
  scripts/_pigen-podman.sh instead.
end note

Operator -> BD : ./build-docker.sh -c config
activate BD

BD -> BD : check for podman\n(grep `podman info` for "rootless")
note right of BD
  **Fragile #1**: even rootful podman
  emits "rootless" somewhere in info,
  so the script mistakenly thinks it
  has to prepend `sudo`, breaking
  rootful-machine workflows on macOS.
end note

BD -> Docker : docker build -t pi-gen .
activate Docker
Docker -> Docker : build container image\nfrom pi-gen/Dockerfile
Docker --> BD : image tagged
deactivate Docker

BD -> Docker : docker run --privileged\n  -v /config:/config\n  pi-gen bash -c '...'
activate Docker

note right of BD
  **Fragile #2**: only the **config file** is
  bind-mounted. ivaliceCluster's stages live
  under ../stages/ and airgap assets under
  ../assets/ — neither is visible to the build,
  so STAGE_LIST=../stages/... cannot resolve.
end note

Docker -> Container : start
activate Container
Container -> Container : dpkg-reconfigure qemu-user-binfmt
Container -> Container : mount binfmt_misc
Container -> Container : cd /pi-gen && ./build.sh -c /config
Container -> Container : runs stages stage0, stage1, stage2 only\n(no custom stage available)
Container -> Container : rsync work/*/build.log deploy/
Container --> Docker : exit 0
deactivate Container

Docker --> BD : container exited
deactivate Docker

BD -> Docker : docker cp container:/pi-gen/deploy/ deploy/
activate Docker
Docker -> Deploy : write *.img, *.log
deactivate Docker

BD -> Docker : docker rm
BD --> Operator : Done.
deactivate BD

@enduml
